.direnv/**

# Beads: the SQLite db and every lock/runtime file stay machine-local (see
# .beads/.gitignore), but `issues.jsonl` — br's own full export, rewritten
# wholesale on every mutation — is TRACKED, so bead state travels between
# machines instead of living only in one checkout. Rebuild the db from it with
# `br sync --import-only`.
#
# The trade, deliberately accepted: two machines mutating beads produce
# whole-file conflicts in issues.jsonl, and br reimports from it, so a stale
# copy can revert a close. Flush before committing, pull before mutating.
#
# ORDER MATTERS, and the first line is not redundant: the machine-global ignore
# (~/.config/git/ignore) excludes `**/.beads/` as a DIRECTORY, and a negation
# cannot re-enter a directory excluded as a directory. So re-admit the
# directory first, then exclude its contents, then name the exceptions.
!/.beads/
/.beads/*
!/.beads/.gitignore
!/.beads/config.yaml
!/.beads/metadata.json
!/.beads/issues.jsonl
